\section{Verification Protocols}

\subsection{Mass Conservation Invariant}

Define:
\begin{equation}
  \Delta Q(t) = Q_{\text{in}}(t) - Q_{\text{out}}(t).
\end{equation}
The invariant enforced is:
\begin{equation}
  \left|\Delta Q(t)\right| < 10^{-7},
\end{equation}
for all timesteps $t$. Violations indicate numerical instability or physical inconsistency.

\subsection{Cryptographic Integrity}

For each ciphertext $C(t)$, integrity is monitored via:
\begin{itemize}
  \item CRC32: a fast checksum for basic corruption detection.
  \item SHA-3: a cryptographic hash for strong integrity guarantees.
\end{itemize}
Stored records include $C(t)$, $\text{CRC32}(C(t))$, and $\text{SHA-3}(C(t))$.

\subsection{Cryptophysical Audit Trail}

The combination of $\Delta Q(t)$, $C(t)$, and associated hashes forms a cryptophysical ledger of system state, enabling forensic reconstruction and tamper detection.

